Mitcad's patch to OCCT 8.0.1, under OCCT's licence:
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

Fillets: a contact of no length is joined with no other, and blends that
come out in no solid of the body are no result (mitcad#1922).

A cube of 10 with its twelve edges rounded by 4.9998: the corners' balls
at both ends of each edge all but meet in its middle, and each face is left
a square 4e-4 wide, its four contacts each 4e-4 long. 0950's
joinEndsAlongContacts takes two contacts on a face for contacts along each
other where each one's points lie within its tolerance (ten times the
approximation tolerance, 1e-3 by default) of the other's: these all do,
whichever two, and 1655 joins their ends inside the face (all its edges
rounded). It then projected the one contact of no length onto the other
blend's surface (GeomProjLib::Curve2d), and the projection walked with a
step of 0: the fillet never returned. Where that projection was stopped,
the builder put the blends into no solid and Compute gave back the cube
itself as done (volume 1000, six faces).

- contactAlong (0950): a contact no longer than ten times the tolerance
  (along the polyline through nine of its points) lies along nothing.
- ChFi3d_Builder::Compute: where blends were computed (the data structure
  has surfaces) but no solid of the body came out of the builder merged
  with them, every solid given back as it was, the computation is not
  done, Failure() Failure_NoResult, with no result shape, and neither the
  grown faces' continuation nor the regularities touch the input's faces
  and edges.

Test: geometry/tests/test_fillet_rib_full_round.cpp,
test_cube_rounded_within_a_hair_of_half_its_side (ctest
geometry.fillet_rib_full_round): the cube of 10 rounded on its twelve
edges with 4.9998 returns (before the patch it ran into the test's time
limit), either not done or one valid solid with the exact shape's volume,
never the cube as done. It fails without the patch: the test does not
build without it (shown 2026-11-20 by tools/occt-port-proof.py).

Upstream: new.
